Track 1: Departure 04:15 (The Fog-Barge Swallows the Rail)
- Story & Context: At the abandoned terminal where the iron train tracks dive directly into the black canal water of Khlong San, Yai Nui positioned her sound-sampan against the rusted engine hull to capture the acoustic frequency of decaying steel. The night air smelled of burning kerosene and sweet lotus syrup as the first sub-bass wave struck, causing the old engine house windows to shatter into the current like fallen stars. A lone French horn played a desolate funeral motif over a thumping 128 BPM disco kick, sealing the pact between the living market-goers and the ghosts riding the rails. Her grand-niece stepped to the microphone, her voice pitch-shifted into a ghost-like shimmer: "The ticket collector has no eyes, but he still asks for your name."
