Track 2: Nam-Keng on the Third Platform
- Story & Context: Deep within the submerged waiting room of the Central Terminal, a ghost known only as Nam-Keng allegedly sits on an iron bench, selling shaved ice laced with liquid glitter to lost commuters. Yai Nui recorded the sound of her brass horn player screaming into a bucket of crushed ice to create the track's iconic, glassy synth lead, which struts over a filthy, sliding 30Hz dubstep wobble. The tension broke when the horn section exploded into a high-energy, 1970s string-laden disco chorus that made the floating market stall vendors weep and throw silver coins into the foam. As the track faded into river ambience, the vocalist whispered the famous platform confession: "I bought a one-way voucher just to watch your shadow stay behind."
