Track 3: Signal-Box Requiem for the Last Conductor
- Story & Context: Legends say the final train out of the valley never arrived because the signalman fell asleep while listening to a floating market sound system in 1978. For this closing epic, the band played three French horns simultaneously through a chain of octave-pedals while dragging heavy anchor chains across the wooden deck of their boat to simulate an approaching locomotive. The track reaches an apocalyptic crescendo where heavy dubstep sub-drops violently tear apart a soaring, melancholic Euro-disco brass melody, leaving only the sound of low tides and distant bells. Over the quiet residual tape hiss, an old radio broadcast crackles with the final warning hook: "Do not wait on Platform 9, the tracks have turned to water."
